# React Patterns for Treinoway Web

## Component Structure

Use functional components with arrow functions and `export default` at the end:

```jsx
// ✅ CORRECT
import { useState, useEffect } from 'react';
import { useNavigate } from 'react-router-dom';
import { useAuth } from '../contexts/AuthContext';
import api from '../api/axios';

const ComponentName = () => {
  // Component logic here
  return <div>...</div>;
};

export default ComponentName;

// ❌ WRONG
export default function ComponentName() {
  return <div>...</div>;
}

// ❌ WRONG
function ComponentName() {
  return <div>...</div>;
}
export default ComponentName;
```

## State Management

Use `useState` for local component state:

```jsx
// ✅ CORRECT - Loading state pattern
const [loading, setLoading] = useState(false);

// ✅ CORRECT - Message state pattern
const [message, setMessage] = useState({ type: '', text: '' });

// ✅ CORRECT - Data state
const [protocols, setProtocols] = useState([]);
const [formData, setFormData] = useState({ name: '', email: '' });
```

## Effects

Use `useEffect` for side effects (data fetching, subscriptions):

```jsx
// ✅ CORRECT
useEffect(() => {
  fetchData();
}, []);

useEffect(() => {
  if (user?.id) {
    fetchUserData();
  }
}, [user?.id]);

// ❌ WRONG - Missing dependency
useEffect(() => {
  fetchUserData(userId);
}, []); // userId should be in dependency array
```

## API Error Handling

Always use try/catch for API calls and display error messages:

```jsx
// ✅ CORRECT
const handleSubmit = async () => {
  setLoading(true);
  setMessage({ type: '', text: '' });
  
  try {
    const response = await api.post('/endpoint', formData);
    setMessage({ type: 'success', text: 'Sucesso!' });
  } catch (error) {
    setMessage({ 
      type: 'error', 
      text: error.response?.data?.message || 'Erro ao processar requisição' 
    });
  } finally {
    setLoading(false);
  }
};

// ❌ WRONG - No error handling
const handleSubmit = async () => {
  const response = await api.post('/endpoint', formData);
  setData(response.data);
};
```

## Navigation

Use `useNavigate()` hook for programmatic navigation:

```jsx
// ✅ CORRECT
import { useNavigate } from 'react-router-dom';

const Component = () => {
  const navigate = useNavigate();
  
  const handleSuccess = () => {
    navigate('/dashboard');
  };
  
  return <button onClick={handleSuccess}>Go</button>;
};

// ❌ WRONG
window.location.href = '/dashboard';

// ❌ WRONG
<a href="/dashboard">Go</a>  // Use <Link> instead
```

## Authentication

Use `useAuth()` hook for user data and role verification:

```jsx
// ✅ CORRECT
import { useAuth } from '../contexts/AuthContext';

const Component = () => {
  const { user, hasRole, isAuthenticated } = useAuth();
  
  if (!isAuthenticated) {
    return <div>Please log in</div>;
  }
  
  if (hasRole('TRAINER')) {
    return <TrainerView />;
  }
  
  return <StudentView />;
};

// ❌ WRONG
const user = JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem('user'));
const hasTrainerRole = user?.roles?.includes('TRAINER');
```

## Event Handlers

Name event handlers with `handle` prefix:

```jsx
// ✅ CORRECT
const handleClick = () => { /* ... */ };
const handleSubmit = async (e) => { 
  e.preventDefault();
  /* ... */ 
};
const handleInputChange = (e) => {
  setFormData({ ...formData, [e.target.name]: e.target.value });
};

// ❌ WRONG
const onClick = () => { /* ... */ };
const submit = () => { /* ... */ };
```

## Conditional Rendering

Use logical operators and ternaries for conditional rendering:

```jsx
// ✅ CORRECT
{loading && <div>Carregando...</div>}
{message.text && (
  <div className={`alert ${message.type === 'success' ? 'alert-success' : 'alert-error'}`}>
    {message.text}
  </div>
)}

// ✅ CORRECT - Ternary for simple conditions
{hasRole('TRAINER') ? <TrainerView /> : <StudentView />}

// ❌ WRONG - Unnecessary conditional
{loading === true && <div>Loading...</div>}

// ❌ WRONG - Complex logic in JSX
{loading ? <div>Loading...</div> : data.length > 0 ? <List /> : <Empty />}
// Better: Extract to variable or early return
```

## Form Handling

Use controlled components for forms:

```jsx
// ✅ CORRECT
const [formData, setFormData] = useState({ email: '', password: '' });

const handleChange = (e) => {
  setFormData({ ...formData, [e.target.name]: e.target.value });
};

const handleSubmit = async (e) => {
  e.preventDefault();
  // API call here
};

return (
  <form onSubmit={handleSubmit}>
    <input
      type="email"
      name="email"
      value={formData.email}
      onChange={handleChange}
      className="form-input"
    />
    <button type="submit" disabled={loading}>
      {loading ? 'Enviando...' : 'Enviar'}
    </button>
  </form>
);
```

## Loading States

Disable interactive elements during loading:

```jsx
// ✅ CORRECT
<button onClick={handleSubmit} disabled={loading} className="btn-primary">
  {loading ? 'Carregando...' : 'Salvar'}
</button>

<input
  type="text"
  disabled={loading}
  value={formData.name}
  onChange={handleChange}
/>

// ❌ WRONG - No loading state
<button onClick={handleSubmit}>Salvar</button>
```

## Component Organization

Organize component code in this order:

1. Imports
2. Component definition
3. Hooks (useState, useEffect, custom hooks)
4. Event handlers and helper functions
5. Render/return

```jsx
// ✅ CORRECT
import { useState, useEffect } from 'react';
import { useAuth } from '../contexts/AuthContext';
import api from '../api/axios';

const Component = () => {
  // 1. Hooks
  const { user } = useAuth();
  const [loading, setLoading] = useState(false);
  const [data, setData] = useState([]);
  
  useEffect(() => {
    fetchData();
  }, []);
  
  // 2. Event handlers
  const fetchData = async () => {
    setLoading(true);
    try {
      const response = await api.get('/endpoint');
      setData(response.data);
    } catch (error) {
      console.error(error);
    } finally {
      setLoading(false);
    }
  };
  
  const handleDelete = async (id) => {
    // Delete logic
  };
  
  // 3. Render
  return <div>...</div>;
};

export default Component;
```
